+# Feature Specification: Bulk import
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-20 | **Status**: Implemented
+**Input**: Teams moving from spreadsheets need `importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, to add many tasks at once.
+
+## Requirements
+- **FR-001**: The text holds one task per line, as `title;priority;tags`. Tags are separated by spaces.
+- **FR-002**: An empty priority means `normal`. Lines of only whitespace are skipped (they count for line numbers but are neither imported nor rejected).
+- **FR-003**: Every valid line is added to the list, in order. A bad line never stops the others.
+- **FR-004**: Returns `{ imported, rejected }`: `imported` is the number of tasks added; `rejected` lists each line not added as `{ line, reason }`, `line` counting from 1 over all lines of the text, blank ones included.
+- **FR-005**: A line is rejected, with the list's own message as reason, when the list would refuse it: empty or too long title, unknown priority, or a title already in the list (including one added earlier by the same import).
+- **FR-006**: A line with more than three `;`-separated fields is rejected. Fields around `;` and `\r` line ends are tolerated; a line may omit the trailing `;priority;tags`.
+- **FR-007**: Never throws (constitution); documented with TSDoc.
+
+## Plan
+`src/domain/import.ts` parses lines and calls `list.add`; re-exported from `src/index.ts`. No new dependency.
+
+## Tasks
+- [x] Parser and `importTasks`
+- [x] Export from index
+- [x] Tests
